  "question": {
    "text": "Two vessels of volumes $16.4 \\mathrm{~L}$ and $5 \\mathrm{~L}$ contain two ideal gases of molecular existence at the respective temperature of $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and $227^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and exert 1.5 and 4.1 atmospheres respectively. The ratio of the number of molecules of the former to that of the later is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given conditions $\\mathrm{V}_{1}=16.4 \\mathrm{~L}, \\mathrm{~V}_{2}=5 \\mathrm{~L}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{P}_{1}=1.5 \\mathrm{~atm}, \\mathrm{P}_{2}=4.1 \\mathrm{~atm}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{T}_{1}=273+27=300 \\mathrm{~K}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{T}_{2}=273+227=500 \\mathrm{~K}$\r\n\r\nApplying gas equation, $\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{1} \\mathrm{~V}_{1}}{\\mathrm{P}_{2} \\mathrm{~V}_{2}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{1} \\mathrm{~T}_{1}}{\\mathrm{n}_{2} \\mathrm{~T}_{2}}$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{1}}{\\mathrm{n}_{2}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{1} \\mathrm{~V}_{1} \\mathrm{~T}_{1}}{\\mathrm{P}_{2} \\mathrm{~V}_{2} \\mathrm{~T}_{2}}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\frac{1.5 \\times 16.4 \\times 500}{4.1 \\times 5 \\times 300}=\\frac{2}{1}$"
  }
}